    "The primary and grandest royal palace of the Joseon Dynasty. Located in northern Seoul, its majestic throne hall, Geunjeongjeon, and the floating pavilion, Gyeonghoeru, standing over a serene lotus pond, epitomize traditional Korean royal architecture.": "The primary and grandest royal palace of the Joseon Dynasty. Located in northern Seoul, its majestic throne hall, Geunjeongjeon, and the floating pavilion, Gyeonghoeru, standing over a serene lotus pond, epitomize traditional Korean royal architecture.",
    "Renowned as a UNESCO World Heritage site, this palace was favored by many Joseon kings because it blends seamlessly with the surrounding natural topography instead of imposing upon it.": "Renowned as a UNESCO World Heritage site, this palace was favored by many Joseon kings because it blends seamlessly with the surrounding natural topography instead of imposing upon it.",
    "Unique among Seoul's palaces, Deoksugung is famous for its eclectic architectural elements, incorporating neoclassical Western-style stone buildings alongside traditional Korean wooden structures.": "Unique among Seoul's palaces, Deoksugung is famous for its eclectic architectural elements, incorporating neoclassical Western-style stone buildings alongside traditional Korean wooden structures.",
    "Originally built by King Seongjong of the Joseon Dynasty as a residence for queens and dowagers, Changgyeonggung features elegant, authentic Korean wooden halls like Myeongjeongjeon (the oldest remaining main hall among Seoul's palaces) and is celebrated for its harmonious blending of stone, water, and ancient pine trees.": "Originally built by King Seongjong of the Joseon Dynasty as a residence for queens and dowagers, Changgyeonggung features elegant, authentic Korean wooden halls like Myeongjeongjeon (the oldest remaining main hall among Seoul's palaces) and is celebrated for its harmonious blending of stone, water, and ancient pine trees.",
    "Known as the Western Palace of the secondary royal residences, it served as a shelter during emergencies. It is nestled quietly beside the Seoul Museum of History and offers a peaceful sanctuary of raw traditional lines.": "Known as the Western Palace of the secondary royal residences, it served as a shelter during emergencies. It is nestled quietly beside the Seoul Museum of History and offers a peaceful sanctuary of raw traditional lines.",
    "Rent a Hanbok (traditional Korean dress) nearby to gain free admission! Visit in the morning to catch the guard ceremony at 10:00 AM or 2:00 PM.": "Rent a Hanbok (traditional Korean dress) nearby to gain free admission! Visit in the morning to catch the guard ceremony at 10:00 AM or 2:00 PM.",
    "The Secret Garden requires a separate, guided-only ticket which sells out quickly. Reserve online weeks in advance to secure your spot.": "The Secret Garden requires a separate, guided-only ticket which sells out quickly. Reserve online weeks in advance to secure your spot.",
    "Stroll down the Deoksugung Stonewall Path (Doldam-gil) during autumn when the ginkgo leaves turn brilliant golden yellow. It's open until 9:00 PM for stunning night views.": "Stroll down the Deoksugung Stonewall Path (Doldam-gil) during autumn when the ginkgo leaves turn brilliant golden yellow. It's open until 9:00 PM for stunning night views.",
    "Excellent for escaping crowds and enjoying quiet contemplation. The traditional wooden eaves look majestic against seasonal trees, and the evening lit-up paths around Chundangji Pond offer an unforgettable experience of peace.": "Excellent for escaping crowds and enjoying quiet contemplation. The traditional wooden eaves look majestic against seasonal trees, and the evening lit-up paths around Chundangji Pond offer an unforgettable experience of peace.",
    "Admission is completely free. Its quiet, uncrowded courtyard makes it perfect for photography of classic wooden eaves and stone steps.": "Admission is completely free. Its quiet, uncrowded courtyard makes it perfect for photography of classic wooden eaves and stone steps.",
