    "The ultimate pinnacle of Baekje art, metal gilding, and Taoist cosmology": "The ultimate pinnacle of Baekje art, metal gilding, and Taoist cosmology",
    "A monumental, spherical white porcelain jar crafted during the mid-to-late Joseon Dynasty. Rather than showing flawless geometry, the Moon Jar is formed by joining two separate wheel-thrown halves, resulting in a gentle, organic, and beautifully asymmetrical shape resembling a full moon.": "A monumental, spherical white porcelain jar crafted during the mid-to-late Joseon Dynasty. Rather than showing flawless geometry, the Moon Jar is formed by joining two separate wheel-thrown halves, resulting in a gentle, organic, and beautifully asymmetrical shape resembling a full moon.",
    "Discovered in the massive tumuli tombs of Gyeongju, these breathtaking crowns are made of pure sheet gold, adorned with complex jade comma-shaped beads (gogok) and tiny golden spangles. They symbolize the sacred cosmic tree connecting heaven and earth.": "Discovered in the massive tumuli tombs of Gyeongju, these breathtaking crowns are made of pure sheet gold, adorned with complex jade comma-shaped beads (gogok) and tiny golden spangles. They symbolize the sacred cosmic tree connecting heaven and earth.",
    "A crowning architectural masterpiece of the Golden Age of Buddhist art in the Silla Kingdom. It features stone terraces, staircases of exquisite stone masonry, and twin pagodas, Seokgatap and Dabotap, which stand as towering emblems of classical symmetry and Buddhist cosmological ideals.": "A crowning architectural masterpiece of the Golden Age of Buddhist art in the Silla Kingdom. It features stone terraces, staircases of exquisite stone masonry, and twin pagodas, Seokgatap and Dabotap, which stand as towering emblems of classical symmetry and Buddhist cosmological ideals.",
    "The original document describing 'Hangeul'—the native phonetic script of Korea, commissioned by King Sejong the Great in 1443. Designed to be easily learned by the common people, its elegant alphabetic letters mimic the vocal organs during speech, representing one of the most scientific scripts in human history.": "The original document describing 'Hangeul'—the native phonetic script of Korea, commissioned by King Sejong the Great in 1443. Designed to be easily learned by the common people, its elegant alphabetic letters mimic the vocal organs during speech, representing one of the most scientific scripts in human history.",
    "A breathtaking volcanic island cluster situated in the East Sea of South Korea, designated as Natural Monument No. 336. Formed millions of years ago by deep-ocean volcanic eruptions, it features dramatic vertical basalt cliffs and pristine, rich marine ecosystems. Recorded historically as Korean territory since the Silla Dynasty (512 AD) when General Isabu integrated the island kingdom of Usan-guk, Dokdo remains a beloved, eternal symbol of Korea's beautiful geography and sovereign pride.": "A breathtaking volcanic island cluster situated in the East Sea of South Korea, designated as Natural Monument No. 336. Formed millions of years ago by deep-ocean volcanic eruptions, it features dramatic vertical basalt cliffs and pristine, rich marine ecosystems. Recorded historically as Korean territory since the Silla Dynasty (512 AD) when General Isabu integrated the island kingdom of Usan-guk, Dokdo remains a beloved, eternal symbol of Korea's beautiful geography and sovereign pride.",
    "Crafted during the Goryeo Dynasty, these ceramics are famous worldwide for their mystical 'bisak' (jade-green) glaze and advanced inlay technique (sanggam), where designs are carved into the clay and filled with black or white slip before firing.": "Crafted during the Goryeo Dynasty, these ceramics are famous worldwide for their mystical 'bisak' (jade-green) glaze and advanced inlay technique (sanggam), where designs are carved into the clay and filled with black or white slip before firing.",
    "Characterized by minimal decoration, low heights to match floor-sitting culture, and focus on the natural grains of premium wood (like persimmon and paulownia). These furniture items reflect the Neo-Confucian ideals of frugality and scholarly composure.": "Characterized by minimal decoration, low heights to match floor-sitting culture, and focus on the natural grains of premium wood (like persimmon and paulownia). These furniture items reflect the Neo-Confucian ideals of frugality and scholarly composure.",
    "A masterpiece of East Asian bronze casting, this incense burner features a dragon-shaped base supporting a blooming lotus bowl, which in turn holds a sacred Taoist mountain peak topped by a phoenix. It represents the exquisite metalwork and religious harmony of the ancient Baekje Kingdom.": "A masterpiece of East Asian bronze casting, this incense burner features a dragon-shaped base supporting a blooming lotus bowl, which in turn holds a sacred Taoist mountain peak topped by a phoenix. It represents the exquisite metalwork and religious harmony of the ancient Baekje Kingdom.",
