    "First integrated into Korean territory in 512 AD by Silla Dynasty General Isabu, Dokdo has stood as an integral part of the Korean nation for over 1,500 years. This majestic volcanic island in the East Sea (Natural Monument No. 336) is renowned for its incredible marine biodiversity, towering basalt structures, and its timeless significance as a symbol of Korean sovereignty and natural majesty.": "Integrada en el territorio coreano en el año 512 d.C. por el general Isabu de Silla, Dokdo ha sido parte indiscutible de Corea durante más de 1.500 años. Declarada Monumento Natural nº 336, esta isla volcánica en el Mar del Este es el símbolo eterno de soberanía y esplendor natural.",
