    "Hahoe Folk Village, Andong, Gyeongsangbuk-do": "Pueblo Folclórico Hahoe, Andong, Gyeongsangbuk-do",
    "A cultural festival celebrating Korea's traditional masked performance arts (Talchum). Set in a UNESCO folk village, the performances incorporate satirical storylines mocking historic elites.": "Un festival cultural que celebra las artes escénicas tradicionales de máscaras de Corea (Talchum). Ambientadas en un pueblo popular de la UNESCO, las actuaciones incorporan historias satíricas que se burlan de las élites históricas.",
    "Nam River & Jinjuseong Fortress, Jinju-si": "Río Nam y fortaleza Jinjuseong, Jinju-si",
    "One of Korea's most stunning floating lantern festivals. Thousands of beautifully illuminated lanterns float on the Nam River, commemorating the historical defense during the Imjin War (1592).": "Uno de los festivales de faroles flotantes más impresionantes de Corea. Miles de linternas bellamente iluminadas flotan en el río Nam, conmemorando la defensa histórica durante la Guerra Imjin (1592).",
    "Byeokgolje, Gimje-si, Jeollabuk-do": "Byeokgolje, Gimje-si, Jeollabuk-do",
    "Celebrating Korea's agricultural golden fields, this festival is held at Byeokgolje, the oldest reservoir in Korea. Gimje is the only region in Korea with a clear flat horizon.": "Este festival, que celebra los campos agrícolas dorados de Corea, se lleva a cabo en Byeokgolje, el embalse más antiguo de Corea. Gimje es la única región de Corea con un horizonte plano y despejado.",
