    "Jeju Island": "Ilha de Jeju",
    "Gyeongju": "Gyeongju",
    "Busan": "Busan",
    "The Neon-Lit Capital of Ancient Spirit and High Tech": "A capital iluminada onde tradição e tecnologia de ponta convivem",
    "Volcanic Wonders, Haenyeo Divers, and Emerald Waters": "Maravilhas vulcânicas, mergulhadoras Haenyeo e águas esmeralda",
    "The Museum Without Walls and Capital of Golden Kings": "O museu a céu aberto e capital dos reis de ouro",
    "Dynamic Maritime Hub, Coastal Temples, and Sandy Shores": "Centro marítimo dinâmico, templos costeiros e praias douradas",
    "A sprawling metropolis where 600-year-old palaces sit surrounded by towering glass skyscrapers. Seoul is a 24-hour city where tranquil mountain hikes, traditional markets, design centers, and dynamic nightlife districts exist side-by-side.": "Uma metrópole vibrante onde palácios de 600 anos convivem com arranha-céus. Seul nunca dorme, com mercados tradicionais, design e vida noturna.",
    "Korea's island paradise, dominated by Hallasan, an extinct volcano. Renowned for its unique black basalt stones, scenic ocean cliffs, pristine beaches, and the legendary Haenyeo (female breath-hold divers) who harvest fresh seafood from the cold deeps.": "O paraíso insular da Coreia dominado pelo monte Hallasan. Famoso por rochas vulcânicas, praias e as lendárias mergulhadoras Haenyeo.",
    "The ancient capital of the Silla Kingdom for nearly 1,000 years. Gyeongju is packed with massive grass-covered royal tomb mounds, ancient temples, ruins, and the world's oldest surviving astronomical observatory, Cheomseongdae.": "A antiga capital do reino de Silla por quase 1.000 anos. Repleta de túmulos reais, templos e o observatório mais antigo da Ásia, Cheomseongdae.",
    "Korea's largest port city, famous for its energetic coastal atmosphere, sandy beaches, colorful mountainside arts villages, seafood markets, and scenic suspension bridges glowing over the sea.": "A maior cidade portuária da Coreia, famosa por praias animadas, o colorido vilarejo de Gamcheon e o mercado de peixes Jagalchi.",
    "Jinhae Cherry Blossom Festival": "Festival das Cerejeiras de Jinhae",
    "Boryeong Mud Festival": "Festival da Lama de Boryeong",
    "Andong Mask Dance Festival": "Festival de Dança de Máscaras de Andong",
    "Seoul Lantern Festival": "Festival das Lanternas de Seul",
    "Jeju Fire Festival": "Festival do Fogo de Jeju",
    "Jinju Namgang Yudeung Festival": "Festival de Lanternas Flutuantes de Jinju",
    "Boseong Green Tea Festival": "Festival do Chá Verde de Boseong",
    "Hwacheon Sancheoneo Ice Festival": "Festival do Gelo de Hwacheon",
    "Gimje Horizon Festival": "Festival do Horizonte de Gimje",
    "Korea's largest spring festival, attracting millions of visitors who walk under tunnels of over 360,000 blooming cherry blossom trees. The Yeojwacheon Stream and Gyeonghwa Station railway are famous photo spots.": "O maior festival de primavera da Coreia com mais de 360.000 cerejeiras em flor ao longo do riacho Yeojwacheon e da estação Gyeonghwa.",
    "An energetic, wild summer party where locals and tourists slather themselves in mineral-rich mud known for its cosmetic properties. Expect giant mud slides, mud wrestling, beach concerts, and firework shows.": "Uma festa de verão cheia de energia com lama rica em minerais, toboáguas gigantes, concertos e fogos de artifício.",
    "Joseon Dynasty (17th - 18th Century)": "Dinastia Joseon (séculos XVII - XVIII)",
